<title>PORTUGAL: BTA falls, adjusting to dividend.</title>
<headline>BTA falls, adjusting to dividend.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Banco Totta &amp; Azores (BTA) fell 133 escudos to 2,577 as the stock adjusted downwards ahead of its dividend pay-out this week.</p>
<p>&quot;Totta has fallen as the price adjusts to the 129 escudo dividend and a generally weaker market,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>From today investors buying BTA shares will not be entitled to the dividend on 1996 results which is due to be paid on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We think BTA could recover gradually to above 2,600 escudos,&quot; said another dealer.</p>
<p>BTA volume was 122,946 shares.</p>
<p>--Lisbon Editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
